From ae72be310f11d24fd21dc95fcb75888b5f6e6a75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: return HybridApp Classic users to OldDot after required
 2FA setup

A HybridApp user who would open OldDot after signing in is kept in NewDot
until the required 2FA setup is done, but nothing remembered that decision.
The 2FA success screen re-derived it from nvp_tryNewDot, which the Onyx
reset after the 2FA validation drops, so "Got it" left the user in NewDot.
That reset also dropped HAS_LOADED_APP and the personal details while
marking the app as loading, so withAgentAccessDenied unmounted the 2FA
screens and the verify step came back empty.

- Store the "return to OldDot after 2FA setup" decision on HYBRID_APP at
  sign in and use it on the 2FA success screen.
- Mark 2FA as enabled in the TwoFactorAuth_Validate success data so the
  verify step advances without waiting for the next OpenApp.
- Keep HAS_LOADED_APP and the personal details through the login-required
  2FA reset so the 2FA screens stay mounted.

Fixes https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/102437
